+# Combo variant of b9e38dc0 (index 6)
+# combo_spec: D4/0+D13/0
+# Name: 边缘控制像素+像素位置编码方向
+
+import random
+
+import numpy as np
+from scipy.ndimage import distance_transform_cdt
+
+from arc_utils import components_mask, get_bg, neighbors4, neighbors8
+
+
+# Design analysis for the fused D4/0 + D13/0 variant
+# a) Concrete behavior and trace:
+#    - The wall keeps the original half-enclosure geometry and still has a genuine opening direction
+#      determined by its endpoints. Flooding still starts from hidden interior cells near the closed end.
+#    - The visible fill seed disappears. The only visible trigger is one isolated control pixel on the
+#      grid border. Its color becomes the propagated fill color.
+#    - The controlled region is no longer implicit: when multiple wall components share the same wall
+#      color, the solver tests each component separately. For a candidate wall, look at the vector from
+#      that wall's bbox center to the control pixel. The dominant axis of that vector encodes a cardinal
+#      direction. The active wall is the unique component whose encoded direction matches its own opening
+#      direction.
+#    - Small trace:
+#      original: interior seed near closed end -> nearest wall -> wall endpoints give radiate direction.
+#      fused: border control pixel -> for each wall, measure control-vs-center offset -> only one wall
+#      gets a matching direction -> reconstruct hidden interior seeds for that wall -> flood and radiate
+#      with the control color.
+#    - Main difference: the control pixel now simultaneously answers two questions from far away:
+#      which wall is active, and which direction should be associated with that wall.
+# b) Complexity calibration:
+#    - A second same-colored decoy wall is added frequently, but not always, so the region-matching
+#      problem is visible without making every sample crowded.
+#    - Direction is limited to the four cardinal axes via dominant-axis encoding, keeping the rule
+#      learnable from 2-4 examples instead of introducing continuous geometry.
+#    - The generator strongly prefers cases where the control pixel sits on a border side that does
+#      NOT equal the eventual radiate direction, preventing collapse back to "border side = direction".
+# c) Broken assumptions from the original solver:
+#    - "Fill-colored pixels are the BFS seed" is false; the only fill-colored input pixel is remote.
+#    - "The wall closest to fill pixels is the active wall" is false; the solver must evaluate remote
+#      control-vs-center relations across all wall components.
+#    - "Wall geometry alone tells the whole story" is false; the wall still has an opening, but the
+#      solver now needs the remote control position to know which wall is meant.
+#    - "Any non-wall border pixel can be treated by its edge side" is false; the encoded direction uses
+#      dominant offset from the wall center, so top-edge control pixels can legitimately mean LEFT/RIGHT.
+# d) Placement legality:
+#    - Every wall component is generated with the original size/margin constraints and rendered only on
+#      empty background cells.
+#    - The decoy wall is kept disjoint from the active wall and away from the active nominal fill zone.
+#    - The control pixel is placed on an empty border cell outside the active nominal fill zone.
+#    - Obstacles are forbidden on the border and on the reconstructed hidden seed cells.
+# e) Visual observability:
+#    - Across examples, the border pixel's color always spreads through exactly one wall region.
+#    - When a decoy wall exists, only the wall whose center-control offset agrees with its opening reacts.
+#    - Because the generator favors border-side/direction mismatches, humans can see that "which edge the
+#      control pixel sits on" is not sufficient; its relative position to the chosen wall matters.
+# f) Visual cleanliness:
+#    - There is still only one control pixel and at most one decoy wall, so the scene stays sparse.
+#    - Obstacles remain singleton dots and are kept off the border, leaving the control signal isolated.
+# g) Change inferability:
+#    - No invisible ordering by color id is used. The control color is copied directly into the filled
+#      region, and the region choice is supported by repeated geometric evidence across samples.
+# 9) New solver assumptions and generator guarantees:
+#    - Assumption: there is exactly one non-wall border control pixel. Generator guarantees this.
+#    - Assumption: at least one wall component yields a non-tied dominant-axis direction from its center
+#      to the control pixel. Generator searches only among such control placements.
+#    - Assumption: one wall uniquely satisfies "encoded direction == opening direction". Generator
+#      validates this uniqueness before accepting a sample.
+#    - Assumption: hidden seed cells remain background inside the chosen wall. Generator reserves them
+#      from obstacles and from decoy placement.
+
